# Pre-#202 harness scratch locations. The suite now writes to a root
# outside the repo (see Makefile.parley); these stay ignored so a stale
# tree on an older checkout doesn't show up in git status. `make
# test-clean-env` removes them.
.test-xdg/
.test-tmp/
.test-home/
COMPARE-SHA
.openshell/.bootstrap/
.openshell/ssh_config
vision

.ariadne-backup/
.goto

# weave-composed agentic context (written by `weave compile` on apply in the VM;
# no longer the tracked symlink to ../ariadne/AGENTS.md — the #95 cutover bug).
.openshell/.base-image-digest
.DS_Store
/bin/sdlc
bin/

# weave-generated runtime artifacts (lowered by `make weave`, like AGENTS.md
# above): skill symlinks, the merged settings.json (#100 accept-transience), the
# .colima symlinks, and the vm-log.sh symlink. Regenerated on every weave, so
# untracked + ignored keeps `make weave` zero-churn.

# agent scratch debug files
.mdbg*
/construct/generated/*
!/construct/generated/vocabulary/
/construct/generated/vocabulary/*
!/construct/generated/vocabulary/issue.json

# parley writes these beside a doc when applying review edits; they are
# scratch, and #205 saw an untracked one nearly swept into a milestone commit.
*.parley-backup.*

# `:ParleyToggleRawLog` writes per-turn request payloads and raw SSE bodies
# here, beside the chat they belong to. Generated debug artifacts: they
# duplicate the transcript and additionally carry the full system prompt and
# every request field, so committing them publishes more than the chat does.
# Diagnosed #228 from one of these and then had to keep it out of the tree.
.parley-logs/

# nvim runtime state. Ad-hoc `nvim --headless` runs from the repo root write
# here (logs, shada, persisted state); `git add -A` then sweeps them in — which
# is how 8ade807 committed four of them (#214 BR-22). The test harness points
# HOME/XDG elsewhere, so this only catches manual runs.
.local/

# Disposable checkout demo; keep configuration in demo/ tracked.
/demo/workspace/
/demo/workspace.launcher-lock/
/demo/recordings/

